    "text": "An electron of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mtext></math>&nbsp;and electric charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math>&nbsp;is accelerated by a&nbsp;potential difference of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;and then it enters in a magnetic field&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;perpendicular&nbsp;to the magnetic field lines. Radius of the circular path formed by electron is"
