  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Bev</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mfrac><mtext>   </mtext><mi>or</mi><mtext>   </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>mv</mi><mi>Be</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mv</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>mT</mi></msqrt></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>KE</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. So&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>mT</mi></msqrt><mi>Be</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>As the electron has been accelerated from rest through a potential difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> volt, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>eV</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>mVe</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>mV</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>"
